A new tab lists every property of the page that is not what the BCB6 .dfm
says (position/size, text, look), component by component. A row click selects
the control; the reset button writes that one DFM value back (one undo step);
the list compares again after every edit, undo and re-draw.

What is compared -- only what the DFM says AND the page's source gives, in the
terms the page generator (_gen_dfm_abs.py) uses, so the list shows changes
someone made rather than the generator's own conventions:
- Font.Size: the generator writes |Font.Height| - 2 (fontpx); the DFM value is
  shown as "14（Height -16）" and reset writes 14.
- Width/Height a source does not give in px (AutoSize labels are generated as
  "width:136px; ... width:auto") are the text's size: not compared.
- Font.Name inherited from the form's UI font (labels, buttons): not compared.
- System colours (clBtnFace ...): shown by name, not compared.
- Coordinates: a wrapper the generator adds (span.lled around an LED + label)
  shifts the origin; compared in DFM coordinates, reset in the element's own.
  A tab sheet (.pcPane) is the DFM parent, not a wrapper.
- A hidden control (hidden tab / panel) is measured by its style, not as 0.
- The same difference on >= 5 controls of one class (e.g. 612 bold
  TBtnPanelLane on HW.IoSetView) is folded into one "同一種差異" line.
  IoSetView: 3,348 raw differences -> 92 single + 13 patterns.

Also fixed on the way:
- A TPanel's Font lives on its <span class="pnlCap">, a TGroupBox's on its
  <legend>: the property grid now reads and writes the font there (a panel
  font-size edit used to be overridden by the caption span's own font-size).
- setLayout from the property grid threw "n3 is not defined" (an earlier edit
  in this round); now covered by the probe test.
- A command run from a menu gets the Uri / webview context as its first
  argument; the diff command no longer takes it for a designer.

Found, not changed (web author's files): 264 style attributes on 21 pages
write font-family:"Name" inside style="..."; the inner quote ends the
attribute, so the font name and font-weight after it are lost.

Tests: lib 101, probe (setLayout by key / by id on a hidden control, lookAll),
smoke 58, panels, real VS Code 62 -- all pass; sweep of 8 pages.
(tools/wb_serve.cpp changed during the last real VS Code run: another
session's AI(W906-HMI-KEEP) work, not this test; not in this commit.)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
